consent.message:
By agreeing, you confirm that:
• you follow Anthropic's terms, and use the Claude Code you installed and signed in to yourself;
• Breezell may read and use what Claude Code reports about its connection, your account (email, organization, plan, sign-in method, version) and your usage limits;
• what you send in Breezell with a Claude Code model goes to your Claude Code, which works on it in that conversation's folder; when it asks before changing files or running commands, Breezell's auto-approve settings answer, or you do;
• Breezell may read the Claude Code conversations of the projects you open in it, and show them in those projects' conversation lists.
Breezell never reads, stores or passes on your Claude sign-in credentials.

By agreeing, you confirm that:
• you follow Google's terms for Antigravity, and use the Antigravity CLI you installed and signed in to yourself;
• Breezell may read and use what agy reports about its connection, its version, the models it offers and your plan's limits, and, to show its model's thinking and its subagents' work, agy's own record of each conversation Breezell has with it and of its subagents';
• what you send in Breezell with an Antigravity CLI model goes to your agy, which works on it in that conversation's folder; it changes files and runs commands only through Breezell's tools, which Breezell's auto-approve settings answer, or you do;
• Breezell keeps what each conversation gives agy (its connection to Breezell's tools, the pictures you attach) in Breezell's own folder, and writes nothing to agy's own settings.
Breezell never reads, stores or passes on your Google sign-in credentials.
